  "explanation": "Document D1S4 explicitly states that 'String Quintet No. 2 in G major, Op. 111, is a work by Johannes Brahms published in 1890.' This is a direct and unambiguous statement identifying Brahms as the composer. Other documents (D3S3–D3S4 and D4S4) mention String Quintet No. 2 in the context of Beethoven and Mozart, but these refer to different works and composers. The fallible audits confirm that only Johannes Brahms is supported by direct evidence."
